Magicbane isn't guaranteed for Rogues unless they find it (e.g. bones)
or wish for it. Stormbringer comes as a gift or a crowning gift. I
must add that the Staff (yeah, my initial post went accidentally _not_
to this group but to email address) requires 2 hands. I know that
artiwishless conduct and limitations for artifact wishing aren't
necessarily worth discussing when weighing how powerful a given weapon
is, but it's one more thing worth noting.

Leveldraining, btw, has one more nice use. It's possible to leveldrain
Archons to make taming them that much easier. Cornercase, strategy-
wise, maybe, though.

As for accidentally hitting monsters, this is one potential big
trouble. A decent alternate weapon and x - command, especially when
navigating quest home levels, are part of the solution.

